  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "LTS Nb3Sn/NbTi primary magnet technology with YBCO only in CS sub-coils is cost-competitive with full-HTS despite requiring a larger machine (R₀ ≈ 6.6 m at B₀ = 6.0 T vs 1.85–3.6 m for compact HTS)",
      "Chinese construction economics achieve 2–4× lower capital cost than Western analogues, applied broadly across CAS21–CAS26 (especially CAS22 reactor plant equipment at ~44% of capital)",
      "sCO2 Brayton power conversion at 34.7% thermal efficiency is the preferred PFPP cycle (vs. 26.4% Rankine, 23.7% He Brayton+ORC)",
      "CFETR Phase II validates DEMO-class operation (Pfus = 1084 MW, Q = 23.5, fbs = 89%) in the same hardware as Phase I via plasma current ramp to 11 MA",
      "Quasi-steady-state long-pulse operation (75–90% CF) is achievable for the commercial PFPP rather than CFETR's pulsed 0.3–0.5 duty cycle",
      "BEST TBM program (COOL/WCCB/EU options) will demonstrate TBR > 1.1 enabling self-sufficient tritium breeding for PFPP",
      "ASIPP's ITER procurement experience (>70% of China's packages, including Nb3Sn conductors) provides a validated domestic supply chain for the magnet system"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Nb3Sn conductor at $2–10/kA-m vs. REBCO at $30–100/kA-m — 5–10× lower cost per unit length than full-HTS designs",
      "Domestic Chinese tungsten supply (>80% global production) eliminates first-wall/divertor armor material scarcity risk",
      "ITER-heritage Nb3Sn cable-in-conduit and NbTi PF coil technology eliminates new-magnet qualification cost (vs. unproven HTS at scale)",
      "Chinese construction labor and domestic equipment supply chains reduce CAS21 buildings and CAS22 reactor plant equipment costs relative to Western projects",
      "Streamlined Chinese regulatory timelines for state research devices may avoid the Stewart & Shirvan 2.2× fission-style regulatory cost factor"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Larger machine volume at lower field — magnet mass scales as ~R₀^2.5, yielding ~10,000 t total magnet mass at PFPP scale (vs. ~2,000 t at BEST), partially offsetting per-km conductor savings",
      "Four-method concurrent H&CD portfolio (ECRH 15 MW + ICRH 10 MW + LHCD 10 MW + NBI 12 MW = 50 MW) with substantially higher capital and recirculating power cost than single-technology systems",
      "Hybrid LTS+HTS CS design with YBCO sub-coils at 18.8 T peak field — adds HTS qualification cost on top of LTS baseline",
      "TBM program duplication — three competing blanket concepts (COOL/WCCB/EU) under simultaneous test, with PFPP technology selection deferred until 2030s experimental results",
      "State-program extrapolation premium — TEA must span two unspecified design steps (BEST → CFEDR → PFPP) that private commercial-intent designs do not require"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Commercial PFPP design point (R, B, Q, Pfus, capital cost) is entirely unspecified; LCOE estimate must extrapolate across two roadmap steps with no published target",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "CFETR Phase II readiness gaps: divertor heat load Pdiv/R₀ = 32.4 MW/m exceeds ITER guidelines; RWM stabilization at βN = 3.54 above no-wall limit not yet modeled; pellet injection fueling not implemented",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "If PFPP inherits CFETR's pulsed 0.3–0.5 duty cycle rather than quasi-steady-state, LCOE increases 1.5–3× (CF=35% → 336.6 $/MWh vs. CF=80% → 158.1 $/MWh)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Blanket technology for PFPP undecided among three TBM concepts; selection drives blanket cost, TBR margin, and power cycle (sCO2 vs. Rankine) — ~9% LCOE delta",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No published capital cost data for BEST or any Chinese commercial fusion reactor; Chinese construction discount magnitude in fusion context is unverified",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "LHCD alone is insufficient for burning plasma — CFETR simulations show Q drops from 2.0 (NB+EC) to 1.2 (EC+LH only) due to loss of NBI plasma rotation and direct ion heating",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Chinese nuclear regulatory cost framework for commercial fusion is uncharacterized; Stewart & Shirvan 2.2× factor may not transfer",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "China has limited CANDU tritium access; commercial PFPP startup inventory (~1 kg) must rely on international procurement or unproven self-breeding from TBM program",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Full-tungsten first wall + divertor under D-T burning plasma at Q~5 has no precedent; ELM mitigation strategies risk W armor melting and are not yet validated",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "TBM materials (RAFM steel nuclear-grade, Li ceramic pebbles at scale, SiCf/SiC composites at TRL 3–4) lack qualified commercial supply chains",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Helium supply for LTS 4.5 K refrigeration is partially import-dependent for China; shared vulnerability with all LTS fusion concepts",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium permeation through CO2-facing heat exchangers in COOL TBM / sCO2 circuit lacks fusion-specific data; barriers needed but uncharacterized",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
